kind: graph
semantic_diff: >-
  Lands the graph layer of the seven amendments the field root applied to the
  delivered graph between 2026-08-29 and 2026-09-03: three change only the graph
  and land here; three touch only the lead skill and hook scripts (evolution
  contract rules 8 and 9, the advisory-hook omission correction, the lead-session
  identity gate); the 2026-08-31 ceremony-cuts amendment splits - its edge
  narrow_plan_repair lands here, and its re-entry instrument declarations on
  screen_pin_and_progress and preregister_acceptance are runtime binding and land
  separately as revision 2, kind binding. Counts: 31 nodes / 89 edges / 12 checks
  become 32 / 95 / 14; 5 control endpoints and 24 evidence definitions unchanged.
  (1) Severity triage at gate 2: outcome review_campaign_design.narrow_findings,
  check narrow_delta_scoped, and edges narrow_registration_repair,
  narrow_record_repair, and narrow_plan_repair route findings that name only
  increment-plan, design-record, or registration surfaces to a drafter-scoped
  repair on the continued doer thread and back to the gate, instead of a full
  design lap; a repeated finding fingerprint or any ambiguity fails closed into
  the full lap, and the full-lap edge design_findings_to_redesign is untouched
  (its rationale now says full-lap re-entries land at the screen while narrow
  re-entries land at their resolving node). (2) Deletion replaces archiving at
  design re-entry: superseded lap material is deleted from the read path and
  history is the record's one-line revision log plus run state
  (assemble_design_record purpose and activities - the record delta-updates in
  place and superseded lap banners are deleted - record_incomplete meaning,
  design_entry_id state field); assemble_design_record also consumes
  adversarial_review_findings so the record carries the standing findings. (3)
  Per-batch implementation review: node review_increment_batch
  (adversarial_reviewer, fresh seat per batch, read-only; outcomes batch_sound /
  material_findings / design_contradicted), check batch_review_current
  (lead-mechanical, on passed_to_next_scoping and plan_satisfied_to_recording,
  on_failure_route review_increment_batch), edges batch_sound_to_scoping,
  batch_findings_to_repair -> scope_next_increment, and batch_review_to_redesign
  -> screen_pin_and_progress; adversarial_review_findings gains a producer,
  increment_lap_record carries the open batch and the size call, and
  review_implementation narrows to cross-increment integration. Price: one fresh
  adversarial_reviewer seat per 1-3 landed increments - in the first run's shape,
  roughly twenty to fifty-five seats per campaign - approved with this landing
  under rule 6's budget item. Why these hold for runs in general: a repair scoped
  to the surfaces a finding names cannot regress surfaces it never touched; an
  archive nobody reads is state ceremony the document budget forbids; and a graph
  that reviews a whole campaign once at its end cannot catch a defect while it is
  still one commit deep, whatever the campaign. No existing check changes; two
  existing edges gain a check.
envelope_check: changed_with_approval
plan_evidence: verified
usage_evidence: field
changelog_entry: >-
  Ships the lean graph's graph layer as revision 1 (32 nodes, 95 edges, 14
  checks): gate 2 narrow triage with drafter-scoped repair, deletion instead of
  archiving at design re-entry, and a per-batch implementation review node with
  its check. Field evidence from the first parity run: 55 increments (57 commits)
  landed with zero implementation review because the graph reviewed the changeset
  once at plan_satisfied, and an external review of the same code then produced
  five repair increments. A run pinned to revision 0 gets exit 3 from verify at its
  next resume and continues on the ledger head per evolution contract rule 7, with
  a backfill duty per landed increment the new gate never saw.
