+    review_increment_batch:
+      intent: review
+      instance_per: approved_campaigns
+      purpose: >-
+        Adversarial, material-findings-only review of one batch of 1-3 landed increment
+        commits before the next scope lap, so a defect is caught while its dependents
+        are still unbuilt. The lead composes the batch and records its size call in the
+        lap record - 1 for a complex commit (a new kernel, runner, scheduler, or
+        weight-loading change), up to 3 when the commits are low complexity in
+        aggregate (config, tests, wiring, citation repairs). A fresh reviewer per batch,
+        independent of the realizer, reads the batch diff, its evidence records, and the
+        plan blocks or ledger rows it claims to realize. Material means - the code does
+        not do what its block declares; the acceptance is hollow (it would pass on wrong
+        code); a frozen or registered value moved (P9); a kernel-class item rides a torch
+        substitute, or a non-kernel declaration hides kernel-class substance (the
+        kernel-substrate rule); an NxDI import on added lines (P4); or an integration
+        defect against already-landed work. Every material finding carries the
+        fingerprint triple (increment id + surface + defect class) the no-progress
+        detector keys on; the artifact-layout impl/review pair entry is the shape
+        authority. Narrow findings (cite hygiene, wording, evidence formatting) are
+        recorded in the same file and route nowhere. Read-only on the worktree and
+        branch; no host execution. Out of scope - any code change, any edit to the
+        plan or the design record.
+      roles:
+      - adversarial_reviewer
+      consumes:
+      - increment_evidence_records
+      - increment_lap_record
+      - campaign_design_record
+      produces:
+      - adversarial_review_findings
+      forbidden_effects:
+      - Any write to the campaign worktree source tree or any branch.
+      - Any write to the increment plan, the design record, or run state.
+      - Host execution of any kind.
+      outcomes:
+        batch_sound:
+          meaning: No material finding stands over the batch; the findings record
+            names the commits reviewed and records the absence. Routes back to scoping.
+          required_evidence:
+          - adversarial_review_findings
+        material_findings:
+          meaning: Named material defects in the batch, each with its fingerprint
+            triple; routes to scoping, which mints the repair items that answer them.
+            Repair commits are reviewed in a later batch.
+          required_evidence:
+          - adversarial_review_findings
+        design_contradicted:
